# Dual remote push

Whenever pushing git branches for this repository, push to **both** remotes:

- `origin` → `https://github.com/puyuheng-git/oa-agent-chat` (GitHub)
- `gitlab` → `ssh://git@gitlab.dev.xkmking.com:2222/frontend/oa-agent.git` (GitLab)

`origin` is configured with two push URLs so `git push -u origin <branch>` should update both. If a push only succeeds on one remote, explicitly push the other:

```bash
git push -u origin <branch-name>
git push -u gitlab <branch-name>
```

Do not consider a push complete until both remotes have the branch tip, unless one remote is unreachable after retries.
